# R23 Letters Home (side quest, delivery): Geneva's last letters, one of them Walder Pye's. By hand, polished by Gemini, unvoiced.

~ start
geneva_fairchild [neutral]: The post will not run tomorrow, nor for a while, I think. These are last letters, everyone's. Each one has someone in the Round to read it. Will you carry them? I would, but I must stay with the cart.
give wv_last_letters
set wv_letters_asked
quest letters_home asked
-> menu

~ menu
* Ask who the letters are for -> who
* [if flag.letters_n >= 3] Tell her they have all been read -> done
* [ends:letters_home] Say there is nothing to be done with them -> unsent
* Take the satchel and go -> END

~ who
geneva_fairchild [neutral]: Sergeant Gaunt has one from his mother. Mr Quill has one from a publisher. Miss Ledger has one from the county seat. Mrs Grey has one from Walder Pye, a traveller who died, and it should go to her in his own words.
-> menu

~ progress
geneva_fairchild [neutral]: Have you found them all? I am counting the pile.
-> menu

~ after
if quest.letters_home == delivered
geneva_fairchild [smile]: The pile is empty. I did not think it could be. Thank you.
else
geneva_fairchild [sad]: The letters are on the board. The wind is turning them. I cannot bear to look.
endif
-> END

~ done
geneva_fairchild [smile]: Every one of them read. Thank you. I will tell the post they were delivered.
take wv_last_letters
quest letters_home delivered
set letters_done
inspiration party
-> END

~ unsent
geneva_fairchild [sad]: Then I will pin them to the board where the wind can read them.
take wv_last_letters
quest letters_home unsent
set letters_done
-> END

~ cart
Narrator: A post cart half-empty of letters and half-full of lanterns. A pigeon's feather, a stamp, a spool of twine. Geneva has a list on a clipboard, and ticks it each time a letter is out of her hands.
-> END

~ to_gaunt
Narrator: Sergeant Gaunt breaks the seal, reads a line, and goes the colour of lard.
sgt_gaunt [afraid]: My mother says come home, and that I am a coward, and that she has always known it. She says she is proud of me anyway. She is the only person who has ever seen me clearly, and I would like it noted that she is also correct.
set letter_gaunt
set letters_n += 1
-> END

~ to_quill
Narrator: Ambrose Quill reads it twice, mouthing the words.
ambrose_quill [sad]: A rejection, from a firm in the city. In verse. It is the best verse that has ever refused me. I shall frame it.
set letter_quill
set letters_n += 1
-> END

~ to_tamsin
Narrator: Tamsin Ledger opens the county seat's envelope with a letter knife and reads it standing.
tamsin_ledger [neutral]: My leave is cancelled, and I am to report back to the audit office by the end of the month. They have not noticed the month is not ending. I shall report that.
set letter_tamsin
set letters_n += 1
-> END

~ to_marianna
Narrator: Marianna Grey holds Walder Pye's letter in both hands for a long time before she opens it.
marianna_grey [sad]: He asks me to tell the mare he is sorry, and that he meant to come back for her. I will tell her. She is in the stable. She will understand.
set letter_marianna
set letters_n += 1
-> END
